{"id":"c-natural-hypertrophy--ultimate-hypertrophy-programs-novice","src":"coach","title":"Ultimate Hypertrophy Programs: Novice","author":"Natural Hypertrophy","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/coaches/natural-hypertrophy/ultimate-hypertrophy-programs-novice","desc":"<p>You have to remember that everyone starts somewhere; not everyone is an experienced lifter who has been training for years and built up the serious <a href=\"https://www.boostcamp.app/blogs/does-strength-matter-for-muscle-gain\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>muscle mass</strong></a> that turns heads. That being said, having a program that is designed for beginners that are looking to fine tune their physiques is ideal, and <a href=\"https://www.boostcamp.app/coaches/natural-hypertrophy\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Natural Hypertrophy</strong></a> has crafted the perfect <a href=\"https://www.boostcamp.app/blogs/best-workout-programs-2024\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>training program</strong></a> for someone like that.</p><p>Natural Hypertrophy has created program designed for beginners that helps to build and tone the muscle mass that you need, and that is the <strong>Ultimate Hypertrophy Programs: Novice</strong>. </p><p>This novice program is ideal for lifters who are just starting out in the gym. The novice program has you in the gym <a href=\"https://www.boostcamp.app/blogs/master-your-fitness-3-day-full-body-workout-guide\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>3 days per week</strong></a> doing a full body split that ensures high <a href=\"https://www.boostcamp.app/blogs/high-intensity-vs-high-volume-training\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>intensity and volume</strong></a> combined with ample recovery time.</p><p>The hypertrophy program combines a good mix of <a href=\"https://www.boostcamp.app/blogs/compound-vs-isolation-exercises\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>compound and isolation exercises</strong></a> aiming to establish a strong muscular foundation. Supersets are used in this program to add volume while keeping the workouts short and simple.</p><p></p>","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":4713,"rate":4.196485623,"rateCount":626,"updated":"2026-10-09T23:14:02.797Z","variations":[{"name":"Intermediate Variation","days":["Full Body 1","Full Body 2","Full Body 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":3}],"note":"Barbell Squat or Hack Squat"},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}],"note":"EZ Bar Curl or DB Curl"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}],"note":"Dips or Bench Press"},{"n":"Dumbbell Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"DB Row or Cable Row"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"Rope Tricep Extension or Katana Extension"},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"Cable Lateral Raise or Powell Raise"},{"n":"Sit Up","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"Sit Up or Cannonball Crunch"}]}],"note":"Suggested workout days: Mon/Wed/Fri or Tues/Thurs/Sat"},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}],"note":"BB or DB Overhead Press"},{"n":"Hammer Curl","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Hammer Curl or Reverse Curl"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Neutral Grip Pull-Up","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"x":3}],"note":"Neutral Grip Pull-ups (Weighted) or Neutral Grip Lat Pulldowns"},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"Leg Curl or Hyperextension"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Split Squat","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"Split Squat or Leg Extension"},{"n":"Fly Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"DB Fly Press or Cable Flies"},{"n":"Neck Curl","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":3}],"note":"Neck Curl or Leg Extension"}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"Romanian Deadlift or Barbell Row"},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise